Basic installation procedure.

You need the GNU autotools: aclocal, autoconf, automake, libtool.

If cloning from the git you need to run:

./autogen.sh

Then, you can run the following commands:

mkdir build && cd build
../configure [options]
make -j 8
make -j 8 check    # optional
make -j 8 install  # optional (use sudo if necessary)


The options for "configure" are given by: configure --help
Options that are specific to PolyLib are:
  --enable-int-lib        Build an int library
  --enable-longint-lib    Build a long int library
  --enable-longlongint-lib Build a long long int library
  --enable-extra-suffix   Add bits size suffix to executables
  --enable-threadsafe     threadsafe polylib (enabled by default if a threading library is found)
  --with-libgmp[=DIR]     Build a GMP polylib using the GMP library located in DIR
  --with-doxygen[=DIR]    Location of the Doxygen Distribution (http://www.doxygen.org)


On MacOS, two options are often needed:
1. to find gmp in the brew pkgconfig directory:
    --with-libgmp=$(pkg-config gmp --variable=prefix)
2. if using the library from the build tree directly (uninstalled), to find
   back the libraries at runtime (rpath) you need to specify:
    --libdir=$(pwd)/.libs
